---
title: Flow 4 — Login and Authentication
---
sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant Client as Angular SPA
    participant GW as API Gateway
    participant IAM as Identity and Access
    participant CACHE as Redis

    User->>Client: Enter email + password, click "Log In"
    Client->>GW: POST /auth/login {email, password}
    GW->>IAM: forward credentials

    IAM->>IAM: look up user by email, verify password hash

    alt valid credentials and account active
        IAM->>IAM: issue JWT, create session record
        IAM->>CACHE: cache session (fast lookup on future requests)
        IAM-->>GW: 200 {token, role, name}
        GW-->>Client: store token
        Client-->>User: redirected to role dashboard
    else invalid credentials
        IAM-->>GW: 401 Unauthorized
        GW-->>Client: login failed
        Client-->>User: "Incorrect email or password"
    else account inactive or suspended
        IAM-->>GW: 403 Forbidden
        GW-->>Client: account disabled
        Client-->>User: "This account is inactive — contact an administrator"
    end

    Note over GW,CACHE: Every later request re-validates the token against this cache,<br/>not against Identity and Access directly — keeps the Gateway fast.
